  "statement": {
    "case_for": "I retain optical lattice clocks as my preferred achievement. They turn precise control of atoms into a reproducible method for time measurement and tests of fundamental physics. Their experimental maturity and sustained development support recognition now, while the citation can stay focused on establishing the method. Katori and Ye made complementary contributions to its concept and realization.",
    "case_against": "The historical record should establish the distinct contributions of Katori and Ye and separate the foundational clock method from later gains in performance. The clocks' full reach for fundamental physics is still developing, so the award should recognize the established method rather than imply that every later advance or application is already settled.",
    "responses": [
